// # app/actor — OTP-Style Concurrency
//
// Logline: Actor-based concurrency (spawn, send, recv, restart), channels, joinable pthread-backed threads, and closures. The oodar-native execution model.
//
// Beats:
//   1. thread.c — the joinable pthread slot table (OoThreadSlot type defined inline in thread.c).
//   2. actor.c — the OTP-style actor (spawn/send/recv/destroy) + the cap-RPC (cap_rpc_send/recv use SignCap since v2.1.0).
//   3. channel.c — the typed message channel.
//   4. closure.h, closure.c — the OoClosure type (fn + env + dtor, stack-or-heap). Generic callable primitive, NOT actor-specific. Lives here only because the OTP-style dispatch in actor.c is its primary consumer.
//
// ──▓▓ app/actor ANCHOR ──▓▓──
// :: OTP-style — supervise, restart, no shared state ::
